{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>That is what I spoke.</b> Meaning, that I am not retracting my first statement, and the first statement still stands in its place. And his saying <b>leimor</b> — meaning, I am still saying so." "<b>Or</b> it may say this way: the very reason that you say you came to search for the lost brother — that is the thing I intended in my words that I said to you, ״spies.״ My intention is along the lines of what you said with your mouths, that you came to seek something in the city. And it is along the lines of what they said, of blessed memory (Genesis Rabbah 91:7), that he said to them, ״And if they do not give him to you, what will you do״ etc. — see their words there. And this matter falls under the category of espionage, insofar as they were plotting against the city's inhabitants. And according to this approach, his use of the word <b>leimor</b> is precisely correct, and understand:"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:59.223987701Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}